    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10934" root="خضم" body-key="x">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خُضَامَةٌ</span></b>  <i>A thing that is eaten in the manner
termed</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خَضْمٌ</span>; [see 1;] (K;) as also ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خُضَامٌ</span></b> 
[expressly said to be like <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غُرَابٌ</span>, otherwise it would
seem to be <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خَضَامٌ</span>, like <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَضَامٌ</span>, to which it is opposed,] (TA,) [and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَخْضَمٌ</span></b> , as is indicated in
the K in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قضم</span>, opposed to <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَقْضَمٌ</span> in that art.
(q. v.) in the S and K.]

